      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their cited evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate: the E2-sourced 'financial stability' claim is correctly marked projected (ibca.org.uk is advocacy/institutional but the claim is modest and hedged). E5's benefit-eligibility claim comes from impact.ed.ac.uk/gov.uk which is adequate. The direction 'improves' with 'moderate' magnitude is justified \u2014 the scheme is real and material for recipients but delivery is lagging and the cohort is bounded. No lever_leakage, party_blind, or false_balance issues detected. The rationale correctly distinguishes the marginal Conservative commitment (reaffirming + extending the \u00a3210k interim payment) from the broader scheme already in place."
